# Performance Optimization

## Next.js Performance

### Image Optimization

Always use Next.js Image component:
```tsx
import Image from "next/image"

// ✅ Good
<Image
  src="/images/logo.png"
  alt="Logo"
  width={200}
  height={100}
  priority // For above-fold images
/>

// ✅ Good - Remote images
<Image
  src="https://cdn.floy.ir/airline-logo.png"
  alt="Airline"
  width={50}
  height={50}
  loading="lazy" // Default for below-fold
/>

// ❌ Bad
<img src="/images/logo.png" alt="Logo" />
```

Remote image configuration in [next.config.ts](mdc:next.config.ts):
```typescript
images: {
  remotePatterns: [
    {
      protocol: "https",
      hostname: "cdn.floy.ir",
      pathname: "/**"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Font Optimization

Use Next.js font optimization:
```typescript
// lib/fonts.js
import localFont from "next/font/local"

export const anjomanMax = localFont({
  src: "../public/fonts/AnjomanMaxVF.woff2",
  variable: "--font-anjoman-max",
  display: "swap",
  preload: true
})

// app/layout.tsx
<html className={anjomanMax.variable}>
```

### Code Splitting

#### Dynamic Imports
```tsx
import dynamic from "next/dynamic"

// Component-level splitting
const HeavyComponent = dynamic(() => import("./HeavyComponent"), {
  loading: () => <Skeleton />,
  ssr: false // Disable SSR if not needed
})

// Named exports
const Chart = dynamic(() => import("./Chart").then(mod => mod.Chart))

// With multiple components
const DynamicComponents = {
  Modal: dynamic(() => import("./Modal")),
  Drawer: dynamic(() => import("./Drawer"))
}
```

#### Route-based splitting
Next.js automatically code-splits by route. Keep pages focused and split large features into separate routes.

### Bundle Analysis

Analyze bundle size:
```bash
pnpm analyze
```

Check [report-bundle-size.js](mdc:report-bundle-size.js) output.

## React Performance

### Memoization

#### React.memo
Use for components that render often with same props:
```tsx
import { memo } from "react"

type FlightCardProps = {
  flight: Flight
  onSelect: (id: string) => void
}

export const FlightCard = memo(function FlightCard({ 
  flight, 
  onSelect 
}: FlightCardProps) {
  return (
    <div onClick={() => onSelect(flight.id)}>
      {flight.airline.name}
    </div>
  )
})
```

#### useMemo
For expensive calculations:
```tsx
import { useMemo } from "react"

function FlightList({ flights, filters }: Props) {
  // ✅ Good - memoize expensive filtering
  const filteredFlights = useMemo(() => {
    return flights
      .filter(f => f.price >= filters.minPrice && f.price <= filters.maxPrice)
      .sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price)
  }, [flights, filters.minPrice, filters.maxPrice])
  
  // ❌ Bad - recalculates on every render
  // const filteredFlights = flights.filter(...)
  
  return <>{filteredFlights.map(...)}</>
}
```

#### useCallback
For functions passed to memoized children:
```tsx
import { useCallback } from "react"

function ParentComponent() {
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>(null)
  
  // ✅ Good - stable reference
  const handleSelect = useCallback((id: string) => {
    setSelected(id)
    logAnalytics("flight_selected", { id })
  }, []) // No dependencies - function never changes
  
  // ❌ Bad - new function every render
  // const handleSelect = (id: string) => { ... }
  
  return (
    <>
      {flights.map(flight => (
        <MemoizedFlightCard 
          key={flight.id}
          flight={flight}
          onSelect={handleSelect} // Stable reference
        />
      ))}
    </>
  )
}
```

### Virtual Lists

For long lists, use virtualization:
```tsx
import { useVirtualizer } from "@tanstack/react-virtual"

function VirtualFlightList({ flights }: { flights: Flight[] }) {
  const parentRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)
  
  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({
    count: flights.length,
    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,
    estimateSize: () => 120, // Estimated item height
    overscan: 5 // Render extra items
  })
  
  return (
    <div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: "600px", overflow: "auto" }}>
      <div
        style={{
          height: `${virtualizer.getTotalSize()}px`,
          position: "relative"
        }}
      >
        {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map(virtualItem => (
          <div
            key={virtualItem.key}
            style={{
              position: "absolute",
              top: 0,
              left: 0,
              width: "100%",
              transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`
            }}
          >
            <FlightCard flight={flights[virtualItem.index]} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Data Fetching Performance

### Server Components (Default)

Use server components for data that doesn't need client interactivity:
```tsx
// app/flights/page.tsx
// No "use client" - this is a Server Component

async function getFlights() {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/flights", {
    next: { revalidate: 60 } // Cache for 60 seconds
  })
  return res.json()
}

export default async function FlightsPage() {
  const flights = await getFlights()
  return <FlightList flights={flights} />
}
```

### TanStack Query (Client Components)

Efficient client-side data fetching:
```tsx
"use client"

import { useQuery } from "@tanstack/react-query"

function FlightSearch({ params }: Props) {
  const { data, isLoading } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ["flights", params],
    queryFn: () => fetchFlights(params),
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
    gcTime: 10 * 60 * 1000, // 10 minutes (formerly cacheTime)
    refetchOnWindowFocus: false, // Avoid unnecessary refetches
    refetchOnMount: false
  })
  
  // ...
}
```

### Prefetching

```tsx
import { prefetch } from "@tanstack/react-query"

// Prefetch on hover
<Link
  href="/flights/THR-MHD"
  onMouseEnter={() => {
    prefetch(["flight", "THR-MHD"], () => fetchFlight("THR-MHD"))
  }}
>
  View Details
</Link>

// Prefetch in server component
async function PrefetchWrapper() {
  await queryClient.prefetchQuery({
    queryKey: ["flights"],
    queryFn: fetchFlights
  })
  
  return <HydrationBoundary state={dehydrate(queryClient)}>
    <ClientComponent />
  </HydrationBoundary>
}
```

## Rendering Performance

### Avoid Unnecessary Re-renders

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - creates new object every render
<Component style={{ padding: 10 }} />

// ✅ Good - stable reference
const style = { padding: 10 }
<Component style={style} />

// ❌ Bad - creates new array every render
<Component data={[1, 2, 3]} />

// ✅ Good - defined outside component
const DEFAULT_DATA = [1, 2, 3]
<Component data={DEFAULT_DATA} />
```

### Optimize Context

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - entire context re-renders on any change
const value = { user, setUser, theme, setTheme, notifications }
<AppContext.Provider value={value}>

// ✅ Good - split contexts by update frequency
<UserContext.Provider value={{ user, setUser }}>
  <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, setTheme }}>
    <NotificationsContext.Provider value={notifications}>
```

### Lazy State Initialization

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - expensive computation on every render
const [data, setData] = useState(expensiveComputation())

// ✅ Good - only runs once
const [data, setData] = useState(() => expensiveComputation())
```

## Network Performance

### Request Optimization

```typescript
// Parallel requests
const [flights, airlines, airports] = await Promise.all([
  fetchFlights(),
  fetchAirlines(),
  fetchAirports()
])

// Sequential only when dependent
const flights = await fetchFlights()
const details = await fetchFlightDetails(flights[0].id)
```

### Request Deduplication

TanStack Query automatically deduplicates requests:
```tsx
// Both components make the same request, but only one network call happens
function ComponentA() {
  const { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ["flights"], queryFn: fetchFlights })
}

function ComponentB() {
  const { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ["flights"], queryFn: fetchFlights })
}
```

### Caching Strategy

```typescript
// Static data - long cache
const airlines = await fetch("/api/airlines", {
  next: { revalidate: 86400 } // 24 hours
})

// Dynamic data - short cache
const flights = await fetch("/api/flights", {
  next: { revalidate: 60 } // 1 minute
})

// Real-time data - no cache
const availability = await fetch("/api/availability", {
  cache: "no-store"
})
```

## Bundle Size Optimization

### Tree Shaking

```typescript
// ✅ Good - only imports what's needed
import { format } from "date-fns"

// ❌ Bad - imports entire library
import * as dateFns from "date-fns"
import _ from "lodash"

// ✅ Good - use specific imports
import debounce from "lodash/debounce"
```

### Dynamic Imports for Heavy Libraries

```tsx
// Only load when needed
const handleExport = async () => {
  const XLSX = await import("xlsx")
  XLSX.writeFile(workbook, "export.xlsx")
}

// Chart libraries
const loadChart = async () => {
  const { Chart } = await import("chart.js")
  return new Chart(ctx, config)
}
```

## Tailwind CSS Performance

### Purging

Tailwind automatically purges unused classes in production. Ensure all files are included in [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js):
```javascript
content: [
  "./app/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,mdx}",
  "./components/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,mdx}"
]
```

### Avoid Dynamic Classes

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - won't be purged correctly
const color = "blue"
<div className={`text-${color}-500`} />

// ✅ Good - explicit classes
const colorMap = {
  blue: "text-blue-500",
  red: "text-red-500"
}
<div className={colorMap[color]} />
```

## Monitoring Performance

### Web Vitals

Next.js provides built-in Web Vitals tracking:
```typescript
// app/layout.tsx
export function reportWebVitals(metric: NextWebVitalsMetric) {
  // Log to analytics
  console.log(metric)
}
```

### React DevTools Profiler

Use Profiler to find performance bottlenecks:
```tsx
import { Profiler } from "react"

<Profiler id="FlightList" onRender={onRenderCallback}>
  <FlightList flights={flights} />
</Profiler>

function onRenderCallback(
  id, // the "id" prop of the Profiler tree
  phase, // "mount" or "update"
  actualDuration, // time spent rendering
  baseDuration, // estimated time without memoization
  startTime, // when render started
  commitTime // when React committed the update
) {
  console.log({ id, phase, actualDuration })
}
```

## Checklist

Before deploying:

- [ ] Images optimized with Next.js Image
- [ ] Fonts loaded with next/font
- [ ] Heavy components lazy-loaded
- [ ] Long lists virtualized
- [ ] Expensive calculations memoized
- [ ] Server Components used where possible
- [ ] API responses cached appropriately
- [ ] Bundle analyzed for large dependencies
- [ ] Tree-shaking verified
- [ ] Web Vitals measured and optimized
